{{!
    @template core/login_layout

    Centred layout for login-flow pages (login, MFA, forgotten password).

    Replaces Boost's two-column split with a single card centred in the viewport over a
    full-bleed background. The background and its colour overlay are painted by
    .atrium-login-page in the theme stylesheet, not here, so an administrator changing
    the image or overlay never touches markup.

    The region-main and region-main-box ids are kept because core CSS and behat steps
    both address them.

    Boost hid the login form's own copy of the auth instructions above lg and showed
    them in the left panel instead. With the panel gone they are rendered here for that
    width only, so neither width loses them and neither shows them twice.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * output - The core renderer output object (provides main_content).
    * leftinstructions - Formatted auth instructions, or null when none are set.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "output": {
            "main_content": "<h1>Login form goes here</h1>"
        },
        "leftinstructions": "<p>Sign in with your student number.</p>"
    }
}}
<div id="page-content" class="atrium-login-page">
    {{! The card is its own element rather than a class on #region-main: core styles
        region-main by id, and an id beats a class, so sharing the element would mean
        fighting specificity for every property. }}
    <div class="atrium-login-card">
        <main id="region-main">
            <div id="region-main-box">
                <div class="login-container">
                    {{{ output.main_content }}}
                </div>
            </div>
        </main>
    </div>
    {{#leftinstructions}}
        <aside class="atrium-login-instructions d-none d-lg-block">
            {{{ leftinstructions }}}
        </aside>
    {{/leftinstructions}}
</div>
